ll also be  discussing about the infections caused  by candida  and malassezia so make sure to subscribe  and press the bell icon so you don't  miss out on those videos  now let's understand how these fungi  damage our skin and cause infection  the spores from these fungi penetrate  the skin through scratching  or small cuts on the skin these pores  get embedded in the skin  and there can be various factors that  promote the growth of these fungus pores  in our skin  the alkaline ph wet and warm skin  conditions  poor hygiene contact with pets all are  favorable for the growth of these fungi  when i use the term superficial fungal  infections  it means that the infection is present  only in the top most layers of the skin  as many of you may know our skin  contains four to five layers depending  upon the region of the body  these dermatophytes only affect the  topmost layer of the skin known as  stratum corneum  this layer usually consists of dead  cells in which keratin is present  these fungi break down the keratin  present in your stratum corneum  by producing an enzyme known as  keratinase  and they use that as their food this  causes  inflammation in the skin which occurs  due to an allergic reaction in the skin  against these fungal products our  defense cells start releasing chemicals  that cause inflammation which is the  redness and itching in the infected area  these fungi can not only affect the  keratinized layers of the skin  but also the keratinized layers of our  hair and nails  these layers also contain keratin which  is used by these fungi and this leads to  an infection of the hair and nails  now let's look at the risk factors and  causes which makes a person susceptible  to tinea infections  excessive sweating in areas like groins  underarms can be an important risk  factor  environmental conditions like hot and  humid temperatures provide  more favorable conditions for these  organisms to grow  if you are keeping your body parts wet  for longer durations  the chances of getting these superficial  fungal infection increases  unexposed body parts like feet scalp  skin areas between the toes and fingers  are more susceptible as you keep them  covered  with shoes and clothes they are left  warm and wet which causes these areas to  become a suitable ground  for the breeding of these fungal  infections  improper hygienic conditions of your  household like infected clothes  blankets bed linens or contaminated  places like doorknobs  can also act as a source of infection  now all people are not equally  susceptible  it depends upon the immunity of the  individual and the ph of the skin  alkaline ph favors the growth of the  fungus  people who are low in a certain type of  proteins known as defensins  which is a type of immunity providing  protein are more susceptible to these  infections  and persons already suffering from some  underlying disease like diabetes  have higher rate of fungal infections as  compared to normal healthy individuals  these infections also occur more in  people with an immunocompromised state  it simply means that a person's immune  system cannot fight from infections  such individuals mostly are aids  patients or people who had undergone  some organ transplant surgeries  these organisms frequently attack such  type of individuals  people who take steroidal medications  for some other underlying conditions  like asthma are also frequently seen to  have these infections  younger and older people are affected  more as compared to healthy young adults  now let's talk about the different types  of teenia infections  tinea can be of various types depending  upon the location  of the infection on the body most common  infections include tinier pedis  which is a fungal infection of feet we  have teenia capitis  which is a fungal infection of the scalp  tinea angium  which is fungal infection of nails we  also have teniacrurus which is very  common and it is a fungal infection  occurring in folds o